<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Southeast Asia Treaty Organization</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1954">1954</a>–<a href="/years/1977">1977</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as SEATO, South-East Asia Treaty Organization, Manila Pact</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/southeast-asia">Southeast Asia</a> Treaty Organization was a collective defence organisation created by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manila">Manila</a> Pact of September 1954 to contain communism in Southeast Asia after the French defeat in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indochina">Indochina</a>. Its members were the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/australia">Australia</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-zealand">New Zealand</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pakistan">Pakistan</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philippines">Philippines</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thailand">Thailand</a>. Weakened by divisions over <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vietnam">Vietnam</a> and the withdrawal of Pakistan and France, it was dissolved in 1977.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/southeast-asia-treaty-organization.jpg" alt="Southeast Asia Treaty Organization" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: SEATO officials; SVG by w:Sn1per · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_SEATO.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
